  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Kurarinol may be involved in the regulation of CX-1 through multiple pathways. The first path links Kurarinol to Disintegrin and metalloproteinase domain-containing protein 28, which in turn targets CX-1. The second path connects Kurarinol to prostate cells, which are targeted by a compound with a complex chemical structure, and this compound also targets CX-1. The third path shows that Kurarinol targets SMMC-7721, a cell line that is targeted by Amarolide, which also targets CX-1. These findings collectively indicate that Kurarinol may influence CX-1 through different cellular targets, possibly through shared molecular mechanisms or distinct pathways. The evidence is consistent with a role for Kurarinol in modulating CX-1, but the exact nature of the interaction remains unclear due to the complexity of the pathways involved."
